  "term": "concordance rate",
  "definition": "Concordance rate is the proportion of cases in which two sources, such as a clinician and a decision-support system, give matching decisions or recommendations. It describes how often there is agreement overall, and may be calculated for any acceptable match or for the top choice only.",
